7' ~ Bels. keep walking on!"},{"id":"B196-20","when":"April 1978","p":11,"h":"NOVEMBER 26th 1977 - WIMBLEDON - BELGRAVE OPEN '7'. BON VOYAGE !"},{"id":"B198-112","when":"April 1979","p":55,"h":"Past Presidents / Life Members / Vice Presidents"},{"id":"B200-118","when":"April 1980","p":46,"h":"PAST PRESIDENTS"},{"id":"B213-16","when":"March 1989","p":8,"h":"From THE BELGRAVIAN 25 years ago.... and 40 years ago."},{"id":"B221-23","when":"Winter 1993/94","p":8,"h":"Profile of a President - Alan Mead"},{"id":"B228-110","when":"May 2000","p":54,"h":null},{"id":"B229-08","when":"February 2001","p":4,"h":"Hon. Secretary's Report to the 2000 Annual General Meeting"},{"id":"B229-18","when":"February 2001","p":9,"h":"Frank Jarvis (1907-2000)"}],"photos":[{"f":"crops/B229/B229-p08-walk-match-battersea-1938.jpg","c":"The caption that goes with this photograph in our archives reads:\n\"Walk Match at Battersea circa 1938. Starters include H.G. Churcher, C.E.Churcher, D.E. Brown, A.A.Harley, F. Jarvis, C.W.Redgrave.\"\nOur first stab at actually naming the faces came up with Don Brown (1), Harry Churcher (7), Charlie Churcher (23), C.W. Redgrave (24) and Alf Harley (behind Brown). However, as others have become involved and have cast their eyes over the picture, we are now not at all sure of anyone except Alf Harley. For instance, we are told that Charlie Churcher did not wear glasses and the chap next to Harry, second from the left, may be Jack Rutland If any reader can help us with more specific details of the race then we would be very pleased to hear from them.","id":"B229-16","w":"February 2001"},{"f":"crops/B160/B160-p01-frank-jarvis-cover.jpg","c":"Belgrave Harriers' President for 1966/7 year---FRANK JARVIS.","id":"B160-01","w":"December 1966"},{"f":"crops/B160/B160-p06-jarvis-presents-plaque-to-taylor.jpg","c":"Frank Jarvis presents the retiring President's plaque to Bob Taylor.","id":"B160-09","w":"December 1966"},{"f":"crops/B165/B165-p29-garnet-cup-montage.jpg","c":"PHOTOS by C. McLENNAN The 1968 \"Garnet Cup at Bexley on February 3rd. Frank Jarvis (centre), this year's President of the R.W.A. (Southern), presents the Cup to Belgrave Harriers. Those seen in action are (8) Mayo,(6) Lawton, (3) Capener, (11) Ward, (9) Picton, (4) Cook, (5) Fotheringham. At bottom right, our scoring four join Frank in admiring their award.","id":"B165-52","w":"March 1968"},{"f":"crops/B229/B229-p09-team-1967-frank-jarvis.jpg","c":"Left: Part of the Belgrave T&F Team of '67 pose with President Frank Jarvis at the end of a successful season.\nBack row: Brian King (throws), Chris Keavey (middle distance), Bill Couzens (throws), Don McLean (middle-distance and steeplechase), Frank Jarvis, Nick Head (javelin), Bob Taylor (Team Manager), Bill Dance (middle distance), Adrian Major (middle distance), Alan Black (middle-distance and steeplechase).\nFront: John Mitchell (long jump and sprints), Phil Smith sprints John Martin (throws), Tony Brooks (440/880), Alan Mead 440/880).","id":"B229-18","w":"February 2001"}],"photo":{"file":"crops/B160/B160-p01-frank-jarvis-cover.jpg","caption":"Belgrave Harriers' President for 1966/7 year---FRANK JARVIS.","source":"B160-01","when":"December 1966"},"x":1,"share":{"d":"Frank Jarvis in The Belgravian, the Belgrave Harriers club gazette, 1965–2001: 20 mentions in 16 issues, 2 race results and 5 photographs. Wrote or reported 4 items.","img":"https://belgravian-images.stephendgardner.workers.dev/belgravian/crops/B160/B160-p01-frank-jarvis-cover.jpg","u":"https://stephengardner1.github.io/belgrave-harriers-data/belgravian/read/share/p-frank-jarvis.html"},"legend":false}